From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:30:06 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] ASoC: samsung: abox: do not free the ABOX regmap when
 the component goes

abox_cmpnt_remove() called snd_soc_component_exit_regmap(), which frees
the component's regmap. That regmap is the ABOX device's own, created
with devm_regmap_init_mmio() at probe and used by the driver after the
card is gone (firmware load, runtime PM save/restore). On the phone
(M10.2 A2r) the card failed to register at 0.4 s, ASoC removed the
components, and the firmware load at 21.9 s called regcache_cache_only()
on the freed regmap: "Unable to handle kernel execute from non-executable
memory" in abox_enable(). The same call is in the 4.14 driver; stock never
hit it because its card always registered. The regmap is also freed by
devm at unbind, so the component must leave it alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Iffb58b4761657cfbe562a9c890229460bac47b3d
---
 sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
index eff54b772..ed88497cc 100644
--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -1259,9 +1259,12 @@ static void abox_cmpnt_remove(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 {
 	struct device *dev = component->dev;
 
+	/*
+	 * The regmap belongs to the ABOX device (devm, created at probe) and
+	 * stays in use after the card goes away (firmware load, runtime PM);
+	 * the component must not free it.
+	 */
 	dev_info(dev, "%s\n", __func__);
-
-	snd_soc_component_exit_regmap(component);
 }
 
 static int abox_sample_rate_get(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
